other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/warp-for-oss%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/warp-for-oss%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/warp-for-oss%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/warp-for-oss%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/warp-for-oss%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/warp-for-oss%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/warp-for-oss%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-05-27T13:52:10Z","updated_at":"2026-05-27T13:58:31Z","body":"@tlapik123\n\nHere's what I found while triaging this issue:\n\nThis appears to be a real default keybinding conflict on Linux: `Ctrl+Y` is currently claimed by `Delete all left`, so the internal yank behavior only becomes reachable after that binding is removed or remapped.\n\n<details>\n<summary>Maintainer details</summary>\n\nI concluded that on Linux, the default Ctrl+Y keybinding for editable Delete all left takes precedence over the fixed internal yank binding, so Ctrl+Y deletes text until that editable binding is removed or remapped..\n\n## Triage summary\n\nThis looks like a real default keybinding conflict in the terminal input editor on Linux. The reporter's reproduction is consistent with current code: `Ctrl+Y` is registered as a fixed internal yank action, but Linux/Windows also defaults the editable `Delete all left` action to `Ctrl+Y`.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- The report includes a specific Warp version (`v0.2026.05.20.09.21.stable_03`), Linux environment, shell, and step-by-step reproduction.\n- `app/src/editor/view/mod.rs` registers fixed `ctrl-y` for `EditorAction::Yank` and later registers editable `editor_view:delete_all_left` with Linux/Windows `ctrl-y`.\n- `crates/warpui_core/src/keymap.rs` returns editable bindings before fixed bindings, and `crates/warpui_core/src/keymap/matcher.rs` dispatches the first matching binding.\n- Removing the editable binding persists as an empty custom trigger via `app/src/settings_view/keybindings.rs` / `app/src/keyboard.rs`, which explains why the reporter can make fixed yank work by clearing `Delete all left`.\n\n## Likely owner area\n\nThis should route to terminal input/keybindings. A fix likely needs either removing/remapping the conflicting Linux/Windows default, making the internal yank action editable/visible, or adding conflict/warning behavior that accounts for fixed bindings.\n\n## Duplicate check\n\nI enumerated all open issues and recently closed issues from the repository. I found broad related issues such as full readline support, plus unrelated keybinding hits, but not two likely duplicates for this specific `Ctrl+Y` vs `Delete all left` conflict.\n\n</details>\n\n*This is my automated analysis and may be incorrect. A maintainer will verify the details.*\n\n_Powered by [Oz](https://oz.warp.dev)_\n\n<!-- oz-agent-metadata: {\"type\":\"issue-status\",\"workflow\":\"triage-new-issues\",\"issue\":11743,\"run_id\":\"019e69b4-f260-785c-b8a8-28fe2fb993b0\"} -->","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/warpdotdev/warp/issues/comments/4555144806/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":{"id":3450139,"client_id":"Iv23lizpgNFAfAxEjnMs","slug":"warp-for-oss","node_id":"A_kwHOBEgy1M4ANKUb","owner":{"login":"warpdotdev","id":71840468,"node_id":"MDEyOk9yZ2FuaXphdGlvbjcxODQwNDY4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/71840468?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/warpdotdev","html_url":"https://github.com/warpdotdev","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/warpdotdev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/warpdotdev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https